From e6a0c4162f5cce086de34952cb9b04d045edc6e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: olympia <olympia@xbmc.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:02:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Video] Hold list items back from the thumb loader while
 dialogs use them

[BackgroundInfoLoader] Allow an item to be held back from the loader (7d84f60)

The loader thread sets art, properties and other details on the items
of a list without a lock, so another thread could only read or change an
item safely after stopping the loader. Stopping waits for the item the
loader is working on, however long its lookup takes. An item can now be
held instead, and the hold only waits while the loader thread is working
on that very item. The loader thread puts a held item aside, goes on with
the other items, and loads the held item between them once it is
released, at the latest after them, still the cached stuff before the
lookup.

The observer is now called before the loader thread lets go of the item,
as it may change the item as well.

[Video] Hold the list item while the information dialog is open (acc8d32)

OnItemInfo() is mostly called with an item of the list, and it copies
the item while the thumb loader thread may still be setting its art and
properties. The item is now held back from the loader while the dialog
is open, and the loader goes on with the other items meanwhile.

[Video] Hold the list item while it is managed (fb2d148)

The Manage menu and Choose art write the art and other details straight
to the list item, while the thumb loader thread may still be setting its
art and properties. The item is now held back from the loader while they
are open, and the loader goes on with the other items meanwhile.

Backported to Kodi 21.3-Omega (a3a448d) for the OSMC vero5 build from
xbmc/xbmc#30197 (fb2d148), its three commits squashed. Omega builds with
C++17, so std::find replaces std::ranges::find, and <algorithm> is
included. Omega's Run() walks the items with iterators; it is replaced
by the same RunStages() as upstream, as the stages, the abort check and
the log texts are the same.
